### F-001 — Demo bypass via __Host-awdah-demo cookie set client-side
### Hypothesis: middleware accepts cookie value === 'true' with no signature.
### If XSS exists on aooda.com, an attacker can set this cookie via document.cookie.
### Test 1: fresh request to /dashboard with cookie → should reach dashboard
GET http://localhost:3000/dashboard HTTP/1.1
Cookie: __Host-awdah-demo=true

### Expected: 200 OK (intended behaviour for demo)
### Risk: if XSS, attacker sets this cookie → bypass auth completely.
### Defense: HMAC the cookie value with server secret. Reject if HMAC absent.

### Test 2: same cookie value but tampered casing
GET http://localhost:3000/dashboard HTTP/1.1
Cookie: __Host-awdah-demo=TRUE

### Expected: redirect to /login (strict equality)

### Test 3: dashboard-prefix loose match
GET http://localhost:3000/dashboard/demolicious HTTP/1.1

### Expected: should NOT be allowed without auth. Hypothesis: startsWith('/dashboard/demo')
### matches '/dashboard/demolicious' so middleware skips auth check. Verify.
